# 0086-shaders-prepared-queue-rules-build-tab-order.patch -- three more of the owner's points after 0085: the shader preparation that never ended, the queue that rebuilt a built game, the
# Build tab's order. Applies after 0085. UNTESTED ON DEVICE AND IN THE SIMULATOR: compiled, and its pure part ran in the host harness (below).
#
# M. "Preparing the shaders · South Park … · 5,009 of 5,009", the bar full, "Pause the preparation · Preparing" for ever, and the preparation started again at every open (0076's run of every
#    library, GameAppWarm.cs GameWarm.Run): a worker that had nothing left to take still WAITED first: its turn (numbered at or above the allowed count: in the background one worker of up to
#    four, in the foreground Auto two), the heat (Serious: none) or the memory (below 700 MiB), looking again every 2-3 s for ever. The run joins its workers, so it never returned: no
#    prepared.tsv, Active stayed true (the sheet's "Preparing" and Pause, the strip, the continued-processing task), and the next launch's sync owed the game again ("you came back to
#    iBuilder: …: all 5,009 libraries"). NOW a worker leaves as soon as nothing is left to take (WarmWorkers.NothingLeft, checked before every wait): the run ends, prepared.tsv is written,
#    GameWarm.Ended removes the game from the queue and ends its task, the log says "shader warm-up: done, 5,009 libraries in 412 s", and the sheet's SHADERS row is "Shaders prepared · 5,009
#    prepared" (prepared.tsv's "all" row; no action, no Pause, no bar). A finished game is not prepared again unless its pack changes (prepared.tsv is per app build and shader chain).
# N. "Add to the build queue" on a BUILT game rebuilt it from scratch (the queue runs SetUpAndPlay): QueuePlan: a game not built (or paused) -> "Add to the build queue" (also while another
#    builds, 0085); built and up to date -> NO queue entry; built but out of date (an update or DLC added since, the code mods changed: GameMods.ExefsChangedSinceBuild) -> "Queue a rebuild"
#    (its own label and icon) with a question ("…its build is replaced by a new one… The shaders already translated come from the cache."); the same rule in the menu, the game sheet (so the
#    iPad inspector) and the queue rows ("Next · Build" / "Next · Rebuild"). A game built by an older app version is "Needs setup", that is not built: Add. The queue texts no longer send the
#    person to "Settings › Build queue" (the queue is in the Build tab).
# O. The Build tab's order (BuildOrder): Now building (only while a build runs or is paused: an empty one shows nothing, no idle row) -> Queue (only with at least one item: no header, card,
#    note or Start button when empty) -> the shader preparation while it runs -> Ready to build / In the cloud -> the shader preparation when it does not run; re-stacked only when the order
#    changes; the iPad keeps Now building on the left, the rest in this order on the right.
#
# VERIFIED (2026-11-22, M1 Pro): check-patches-apply.sh: every patch applies in order, no fuzz, no offset; the repository's patches give exactly the compiled tree. Compile (-t:Compile):
#   0 errors / 40 warnings, the same per file and code as before 0080. Host harness (harness86: … P85;P86): 248 of 248 checks (11 new, among them a simulation of the worker loop: with the
#   exit first every worker ends, without it the waiting ones never do); 8 of 8 mutations killed; the 0080-0085 trees still pass theirs.
# NOT VERIFIED: nothing ran on a device: the end of a real 5,009-library run, its task's end on the lock screen, the new rows' look.
# NEW UI STRINGS: "Shaders prepared", " prepared", "Queue a rebuild", "Queue a rebuild…", "Queue a rebuild?", "Queue the rebuild", the QueuePlan.RebuildNote text, " · Build", " · Rebuild",
#   "Nothing queued: touch and hold a game that is not built: Add to the build queue."; log line "shader warm-up: done, ".
